  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th. The initial budget was $500,000, but it was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration. The project aims to leverage AI for data visualization and secure file sharing. Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase and successful prototype testing ahead of schedule. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with an onboarding session on September 10th. A call for ideas from R&D was issued with a July 20th deadline. Additional budgets were approved for compliance ($55,000) and training ($15,000). A celebration for the milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
